677:    // before any user message — so the meter renders a post-cap number
678:    // instead of idling above 100% until the first pre-flight. The
679:    // boundary walk above bounds residency, but a reachable boundary
680:    // whose kept-path projection is over the window (or a giant tail
681:    // record the budget trim floors at) still boots over-window.
682:    //
683:    // Ordered AFTER the gh-1000 binding restore (gh-1425 review): the
684:    // cap's summarizer requests must ride the session's OWN
685:    // provider/model binding, not the launch default — otherwise every
686:    // boot of a non-default-provider session bills (or 401s against) the
687:    // wrong endpoint before the restore lands.
688:    await _capResumedContext(session);
